findings.detail:
@strudel/core@1.2.6 depends on fraction.js ^5.2.1, and `Pattern.queryArc(begin, end, controls)` returns haps with exact rational times. If 1 cycle equals 1 bar (set with setcpm), quantization is exact and tuplets come out naturally (3 events per half-cycle gives a triplet). A TypeScript layer can then:
- split events at beat and barline boundaries and add ties;
- group beams by meter;
- spell pitches with tonal@6.5.1 (MIT, 2026-10), using the key's scale and chord context;
- emit ABC for abcjs or StaveNotes for VexFlow.

Strudel itself pins @tonaljs/tonal 4.10.

In the published superdough@1.3.0 dist/index.mjs (139KB), the worklets are embedded as `const Un = "data:text/javascript;base64,..."` and loaded with `audioCtx.audioWorklet.addModule(url)`. Kabelsalat generic processors also use data: URLs. This works in Bun and Vite without special handling.

The Codeberg source differs. packages/superdough/superdough.mjs on main uses `import workletsUrl from './worklets.mjs?audioworklet'`, which needs `vite-plugin-bundle-audioworklet` (0.1.2). Its package.json has main 'index.mjs' and publishConfig.main 'dist/index.mjs'. Consuming Strudel from a git or workspace source therefore needs Vite plus that plugin; Bun cannot handle it.

@strudel/codemirror@1.3.0 keeps the @codemirror/* packages (^6.x) as external dependencies, so they dedupe with the app's own copies. All @strudel/* packages are AGPL-3.0-or-later. tidalcycles/strudel on GitHub is archived; npm 1.3.0 was published 2026-01-18.

@strudel/transpiler index.mjs: `export const evaluate = (code) => _evaluate(code, transpiler)`.
core evaluate.mjs: evalScope(...modulePromises) copies exports onto globalThis and strudelScope; evaluate(code, transpiler) runs safeEval through `Function('"use strict";return (...)')` and returns { mode, pattern, meta }.
`$:` blocks need Pattern.prototype.p, which is only injected inside repl().evaluate (repl.mjs L170-181). For multi-block code, the grader should therefore build `repl({ defaultOutput: () => {}, getTime: () => 0 })` and call `evaluate(code, false)`. SalatRepl's constructor (class Fe) only creates a Map, and Cyclist only builds a clock, so this should be headless-safe (inferred).
